# C16 (QUALIFICATION): lifecycle churn at eight seats on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-audit WITH PREFIX CACHING ON: 16 sessions over 8 seats (each of the last eight is admitted into a seat a
# departure freed), 1024 tokens out, the last user short (1536); every stream carries its own fresh cache_salt (C2_GATE_SALT=fresh) so each one captures and publishes
# its prefix under chunked prefill, which runs the reservation with prefix caching on in the REAL engine (gap c: the reduced-model test is the only other proof).
# READ: 16 sessions completed, no engine death, no abort, no refusal; every release logged; the RESERVATION HOLD is exercised and RELEASED (the hold line when a long
# arrival waits for DRAM, then its release; a hold with every seat busy is the ninth user waiting, not a failure; a hold while a seat is free is a FAIL); prefix
# captures and releases balanced at the end; the kernel cache +0 programs after the warm. Real time ~45.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the ship/262k-prefix pack (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over that file on a throwaway
# commit of the integration branch (with its evidence files committed) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has
# the order, stop rules, real minutes, NEEDS and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10 is the ONE shipping image X0B builds: every job serves it.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-audit
C2_GATE_PLAN=churn
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=253920,200000,131072,65536,32768,16384,8192,4096,253920,131072,65536,32768,16384,8192,4096,1536
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=1024
C2_GATE_JIT=record
C2_GATE_AUDITS=extent
C2_GATE_SALT=fresh
